{
  "name": "UberLLM: Google Sheet or CSV rows → one image + video ad per row, on a schedule",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Sheet rows → one image + video ad per row, on a schedule (UberLLM)\nEach row of a sheet becomes a still and a clip. Add rows whenever you like; the daily run makes only the new ones.\n1. **Read rows** fetches the sheet as CSV. **Rows to make** skips rows made before and takes at most `max_rows_per_run`.\n2. **Make row still**: `google/nano-banana-2-edit` puts the product in the row's scene, in the row's shape.\n3. **Start row video**: `kling/kling-o3-standard-image-to-video` animates the still (the clip takes the still's shape).\n4. **Rows made** lists every row with its `still` and `clip` as binary data.\nA row that fails does not stop the others, costs nothing for the failed step, and is tried again on the next run.\n\n### Your sheet\nColumns (first line): `name, image_url, scene, motion, aspect_ratio`. Only `image_url` is required (a public `https://` link to the product photo).\n- **Google Sheets**: File → Share → Publish to web → pick the tab → *Comma-separated values (.csv)* → Publish, and paste that link into `csv_url`. No Google credential is needed. Anyone with the link can read a published sheet.\n- Or any `https://` link to a CSV file.\n\n### Setup (2 minutes)\n1. Get a key at https://uberllm.dev (sign in with your email, add credit).\n2. Open any **UberLLM** HTTP node → Credential → **Create new** → *Header Auth*:\n   - Name: `Authorization`\n   - Value: `Bearer YOUR_UBERLLM_KEY`\n   Every UberLLM node in this workflow uses this one credential.\n3. Edit the **Settings** node, then click **Execute workflow**.\n\nTo run it every day, switch the workflow to **Active**. The schedule is in **Every day**.\n\n### Price\nListed on 2026-11-19: 1 still at $0.04 each + a 5 s clip at $0.07 per second per row = about $0.39. Live prices: https://uberllm.dev/ai-ad-creative-api\n\n### What you pay\n- The start reply shows the price now (`estimated_cost_usd`). The bill is what the provider charged, which can differ if the job moves to another provider.\n- Your ceiling is `max_cost` in **Settings**: a job that would cost more is refused or cancelled at no charge.\n- A video that fails or runs out of time costs nothing: the whole hold comes back.\n- Credit you buy does not expire while your account is open.\n- No UberLLM fee on requests. Adding credit by card costs 5.5% + $0.50.\n\n### Files are short-lived\nPicture links are kept about 15 minutes and video links about 3 hours, and they need your key. The workflow downloads every result at once, so the last node holds the files as binary data: send them to Drive, S3 or your ad tool from there.\n\n### Why the still is uploaded\nA result link needs your key, so a video model cannot open it. **Upload still** puts the picture in your UberLLM files (kept 24 hours) and the clip starts from that upload.\n",
        "height": 1320,
        "width": 640
      },
      "id": "0f388fe2-7aad-5b88-80c1-a703b674f865",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -680,
        -360
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### Before you run ads\n- People in these pictures and clips are AI-generated. Label them as AI where the platform or the law asks, and never present one as a real customer or a testimonial.\n- No health claims and no before/after pairs: Meta's ad rules apply whatever tool made the creative.\n- Check the model maker's terms for commercial use, and use only product photos you have the rights to.\nLinks to Meta's rules and each maker's terms: https://uberllm.dev/ai-ad-creative-api\n",
        "height": 330,
        "width": 620,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "74c25f59-2fe0-5cc3-aaa8-46898351e69c",
